<title>USA: Philip Morris sets $750 mln in 30-year debt.</title>
<headline>Philip Morris sets $750 mln in 30-year debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Philip Morris Cos Inc was priced on Tuesday, according to lead manager Merrill Lynch &amp; Co.</p>
<p>The deal was upped in size from an initial $500 million to meet strong investor demand for the issue, dealers said.</p>
<p>BORROWER Philip Morris</p>
<p>   AMT $750	     COUPON   7.75     MATURITY  01/15/27</p>
<p>   TYPE BONDS	   ISS PRICE 99.148  FIRST PAY DATE</p>
<p>   LAST MOODY'S  A2   YIELD     7.824   PAY FREQ SEMI</p>
<p>   LAST S&amp;P	A    SPREAD    101     CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1675</p>
</text>
